@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+# OpenProject BoardUI appearance
+
+The shared theme at `public/styles/boardui.css` adapts the publicly visible
+[BoardUI](https://www.boardui.com/) visual language to OpenProject's existing
+Rails, Primer, Spot and Angular components. The reference is its dashboard UI,
+not the marketing homepage: floating neutral sidebar, blue selection, Inter,
+rounded panels, soft control borders and restrained elevation.
+
+The common head loads one local stylesheet. Inter is bundled locally with its
+OFL license in `public/fonts/inter`, so the installed application makes no
+BoardUI, Google Fonts or other external requests for this theme. React and
+Tailwind are not added to OpenProject.
+
+Coverage: application header and search, main and nested navigation, home widgets,
+tables, board lists/cards, buttons, form controls, focus/error/disabled states,
+dialogs, menus, tabs, pagination and sign-in. The existing theme preference still
+selects light or dark appearance. Semantic status/type colors are retained.
+The blue and muted text shades are slightly darker than the reference for text
+contrast. Existing responsive navigation, table scrolling, resizing and print
+behavior remain in place.
+
+No models, controllers, routes, permissions, field names, form submissions,
+workflow transitions, task data or JavaScript event handlers are changed by the
+theme. The only template change is the stylesheet link. The Windows manager build
+bundles the stylesheet, font and template; repair refreshes the theme code while
+retaining database, attachments and credentials.
+
+This is a visual adaptation across OpenProject's component families, not a claim
+of pixel-identical reproduction of every BoardUI Pro template or certification
+of every OpenProject screen. BoardUI's React components are not interchangeable
+with OpenProject's working controls.
+
+## Verification
+
+Inspected in Chrome on the native Windows instance: home, Projects, Work packages,
+filter toggle, Kanban (11 real cards), new-work-package form opened/cancelled
+without saving, account settings, and isolated sign-in. Viewports checked at
+1440px, 768px and 390px; the page did not overflow horizontally, and the existing
+mobile navigation collapsed. Light and dark appearance were inspected without
+saving user preferences. Inter loaded from the local server.
+
+Comparing the themed and unthemed Kanban DOM preserved all 129 links, buttons,
+form actions and input semantics. Focus remained visible, invalid inputs retained
+their red border, and disabled controls used a readable neutral treatment.
+Primary light button contrast was 4.63:1; the dark button uses dark text on blue.
+The shared-head ERB passed Ruby compilation. No task, account, board or project
+was saved during these visual checks.
